  "description": "Deep dive: longest increasing subsequence in O(n^2) and O(n log n) patience sorting, string chains and Russian doll envelopes, then two-string DP: LCS, edit distance, distinct subsequences, wildcard and regex matching, interleaving string, with steppers and Go/C++/Java/Python templates.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">50 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Dynamic Programming</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>LIS and two-string DP (LCS, edit distance)</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Two families cover a big share of the DP questions asked in SDE-2 and SDE-3 rounds. The first is the longest increasing subsequence: an O(n<sup>2</sup>) table, then patience sorting in O(n log n), then the same idea on string chains and nested envelopes. The second is a grid over two strings: LCS, edit distance, distinct subsequences, wildcard and regex matching, and interleaving. Each one is the same table with a different meaning on its three arrows. Templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\n"
  },
